---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Welder Qualification Certification | Eurocert"
  description="Explore welder qualification certification with Eurocert, including requirements, audit or assessment stages, documentation, certification support."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.eurocert.asia/welder-qualifications/"
  ogImage="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367859/eurocert/Untitled_design_19_.png.png"
  keywords="Eurocert,Eurocert Asia,ISO certification,CE marking,food safety certification,FSSC 22000,BRCGS,GFSI,social audits,Sedex,SMETA,SA8000,inspection services,certification body,India,management systems,ISO 9001,ISO 14001,ISO 45001"
>
<style is:global>@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:900;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-solid-900.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Brands";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-brands-400.woff2) format('woff2')}@font-face{font-family:"Font Awesome 6 Free";font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-display:swap;src:url(https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/webfonts/fa-regular-400.woff2) format('woff2')}</style>
<section class="relative min-h-[55vh] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden bg-[#030a16]"><div class="absolute inset-0 z-0"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367545/eurocert/1.png.png" class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-30" alt="Welding"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#030a16]/70 via-[#030a16]/40 to-[#030a16]"></div></div><div class="container mx-auto px-6 relative z-10 text-center py-20"><div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-eurogold-400/30 bg-eurogold-400/5 mb-6"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400 animate-pulse"></span><span class="heading-font text-[10px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.3em] uppercase font-bold">EN ISO 9606 • ASME IX</span></div><h1 class="heading-font text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold text-white mb-3 tracking-tight" style="text-shadow:0 0 30px rgba(212,168,67,0.3)">Welder Qualifications</h1><h3 class="heading-font text-white/70 text-base md:text-lg uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-4">Testing Procedure</h3><p class="text-white/90 text-sm md:text-base max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Comprehensive welder qualification testing and certification to ensure welders have the required skills and knowledge for safe, effective welding projects.</p><div class="mt-8"><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#030a16] bg-eurogold-400 rounded-full px-8 py-3.5 hover:bg-eurogold-300 transition-all shadow-lg shadow-eurogold-400/20" href="/#contact">Click For Free Consultation <i class="fas fa-arrow-right text-[9px]"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="grid lg:grid-cols-5 gap-10 items-start"><div class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-6"><div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Fundamentals</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight leading-tight">What is <span class="text-euro-600">Welding?</span></h2></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">Welding is a process of joining two pieces of material together by heating them until they melt and then cooling them so that they form a strong bond. There are many types of welding, and the most common is arc welding.</p><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-euro-50/40"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-bolt text-white text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">How Arc Welding Works</h4></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Arc welding uses an electric current to create an arc between two pieces of metal. The heat from the arc melts the metal and creates a pool of molten metal called a weld pool. As the weld pool cools down, it forms a strong joint between the two pieces of metal.</p></div><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Welding is distinguished from other joining processes, such as brazing and soldering, which do not melt the base metal. Numerous welding processes are available, including arc welding, gas welding, and resistance welding  -  each with its own advantages, strength, appearance, and cost characteristics.</p></div><div class="lg:col-span-2 relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-slate-100 h-[320px] md:h-[420px] group"><img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dwnnakrrh/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto:good,w_1600/v1782367545/eurocert/1.png.png" class="w-full h-full object-cover transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-105" alt="Welding Process"/><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-900/20 via-transparent to-transparent"></div></div></div></div></section><section class="relative overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#030a16]"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top_left,rgba(212,168,67,0.05)_0%,transparent_60%)]"></div><div class="relative z-10 py-14 lg:py-18"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Welding Processes</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Types of Welding</h2></div><div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5"><div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 overflow-hidden group"><div class="h-40 overflow-hidden"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504307651254-35680f356dfd?auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80&amp;w=400" alt="Arc Welding" class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-700"/></div><div class="p-5"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-bolt text-eurogold-400 text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Arc Welding</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-xs leading-relaxed">Uses an electric arc to create heat for melting metal. Produces clean welds with minimal slag buildup  -  commonly used where aesthetics are important. Can be difficult to achieve consistent results and is not recommended for large projects requiring high precision.</p></div></div><div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 overflow-hidden group"><div class="h-40 overflow-hidden"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504328345606-18bbc8c9d7d1?auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80&amp;w=400" alt="Gas Welding" class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-700"/></div><div class="p-5"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-fire text-eurogold-400 text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Gas Welding</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-xs leading-relaxed">Uses oxygen and fuel gas (usually acetylene) to create heat for melting metal. Commonly used where speed is more important than aesthetics. Can be dangerous if not done properly due to the risk of explosion.</p></div></div><div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 overflow-hidden group"><div class="h-40 overflow-hidden"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581094794329-c8112a89af12?auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;q=80&amp;w=400" alt="Resistance Welding" class="w-full h-full object-cover group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-700"/></div><div class="p-5"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-plug text-eurogold-400 text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Resistance Welding</h4></div><p class="text-white/50 text-xs leading-relaxed">Joins metals by applying pressure and passing current through the metal area to be joined. Commonly used in automotive and manufacturing industries for spot welding and seam welding applications.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Certification Categories</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">Qualifications for Welding</h2></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8">To become a certified welder, one must pass a welding examination. A welder must have two years of experience in their particular category and pass both a written examination and a practical test.</p><div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-8"><div class="relative p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-gradient-to-br from-euro-50/60 to-white text-center"><div class="absolute -top-3 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><span class="heading-font text-white text-xs font-bold">01</span></div><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mx-auto mt-3 mb-3"><i class="fas fa-building text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Structural Steel Welding</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-xs leading-relaxed">Qualification for welding structural steel components used in buildings, bridges, and infrastructure.</p></div><div class="relative p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-gradient-to-br from-euro-50/60 to-white text-center"><div class="absolute -top-3 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><span class="heading-font text-white text-xs font-bold">02</span></div><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mx-auto mt-3 mb-3"><i class="fas fa-water text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Piping Welding</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-xs leading-relaxed">Qualification for welding piping systems used in oil &amp; gas, chemical, and process industries.</p></div><div class="relative p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-gradient-to-br from-euro-50/60 to-white text-center"><div class="absolute -top-3 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><span class="heading-font text-white text-xs font-bold">03</span></div><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mx-auto mt-3 mb-3"><i class="fas fa-database text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Pressure Vessel Welding</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-xs leading-relaxed">Qualification for welding pressure vessels subject to internal pressure and high temperatures.</p></div></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5"><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-euro-50/30"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-pen text-white text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Written Examination</h4></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Tests the welder&#x27;s knowledge of safety, shop math, blueprint reading, and weld symbols.</p></div><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-euro-100 bg-euro-50/30"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-tools text-white text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Practical Examination</h4></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">The welder must demonstrate proper weld bead location, width, height, penetration, and fusion on plate and pipe specimens.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="relative overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#030a16]"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top_right,rgba(212,168,67,0.05)_0%,transparent_60%)]"></div><div class="relative z-10 py-14 lg:py-18"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-eurogold-400 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Step by Step</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Testing Procedure</h2><p class="text-white/45 text-sm mt-3 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Welding qualifications testing evaluates a welder&#x27;s ability to produce quality welds. Variables include the type and thickness of metal, welding process used, and the welder&#x27;s experience and skill level.</p></div><div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5"><div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 text-center"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><span class="heading-font text-eurogold-400 font-bold text-sm">01</span></div><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-eurogold-400/5 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><i class="fas fa-cogs text-eurogold-400 text-sm"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[10px] font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Equipment Setup</h4><p class="text-white/45 text-xs leading-relaxed">Set up the power source, select the appropriate welding electrode, and set the welding parameters.</p></div><div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 text-center"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><span class="heading-font text-eurogold-400 font-bold text-sm">02</span></div><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-eurogold-400/5 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><i class="fas fa-fire text-eurogold-400 text-sm"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[10px] font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Test Coupon Welding</h4><p class="text-white/45 text-xs leading-relaxed">The welder is given a test coupon (piece of metal) to weld and must produce a weld meeting all specified requirements.</p></div><div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 text-center"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><span class="heading-font text-eurogold-400 font-bold text-sm">03</span></div><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-eurogold-400/5 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><i class="fas fa-search text-eurogold-400 text-sm"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[10px] font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Weld Inspection</h4><p class="text-white/45 text-xs leading-relaxed">The completed weld is inspected for visual defects, dimensional accuracy, and penetration.</p></div><div class="p-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 bg-white/2 text-center"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-eurogold-400/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><span class="heading-font text-eurogold-400 font-bold text-sm">04</span></div><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-eurogold-400/5 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3"><i class="fas fa-check-double text-eurogold-400 text-sm"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[10px] font-bold text-white uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Pass or Fail</h4><p class="text-white/45 text-xs leading-relaxed">The welder receives a pass or fail based on performance. If passed, they are qualified for that material and thickness.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-[#f8fafc]"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="text-center mb-10"><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 tracking-[0.5em] uppercase mb-2 font-bold">Our Services</h4><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">Welder Qualification Services</h2></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5 max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-user-check text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Welder Qualification Testing</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Complete welder qualification testing per EN ISO 9606 and ASME standards.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-clipboard-check text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Welding Procedure Approval</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Welding Procedure Specification (WPS) and Procedure Qualification Record (PQR) approval.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-chalkboard-teacher text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Welder Training</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Comprehensive welder training programs for various welding processes and materials.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-certificate text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Welder Certification</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Issue welder certificates upon successful completion of qualification tests.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-file-alt text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">Documentation Review</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">Review of welding documentation, procedures, and quality records.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 hover:border-euro-200 hover:shadow-lg transition-all duration-300 group"><div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-euro-50 flex items-center justify-center text-euro-600 mb-4 group-hover:bg-euro-600 group-hover:text-white transition-all duration-300"><i class="fas fa-industry text-base"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-900 mb-2">On-site Supervision</h4><p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">On-site welding supervision and inspection during production welding.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="py-14 lg:py-18 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5"><div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-slate-100 bg-[#f8fafc]"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3"><div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-xl bg-euro-600 flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb text-white text-xs"></i></div><h4 class="heading-font text-[11px] text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Conclusion</h4></div><p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">Welder qualifications testing procedures are important for ensuring that welders have the required skills and 